\title{JsonCSVMaskr: deterministic masking for JSON and CSV data}
\description{
JsonCSVMaskr is an R translation of the PowerShell Flat & Mask data masking
tool. It masks selected CSV columns or JSON field paths with deterministic
HMAC-SHA256 values, writes a masking key, preserves a masked JSON copy when
applicable, normalizes nested JSON into related CSV tables, and includes a
Shiny interface.
}
\section{Supported input shapes}{

CSV files with headers; ordinary JSON objects; arrays of JSON objects;
NDJSON, JSON Lines, comma-separated loose objects, and concatenated objects;
Socrata exports with \code{meta.view.columns} and row-array \code{data}; GeoJSON
\code{FeatureCollection} objects; envelope collections under \code{data}, \code{results},
\code{items}, or \code{records}; and top-level header-row array JSON.
}

\section{Masking behavior}{

Masked values are an \code{x} prefix followed by the first 12 Base64 characters of
an HMAC-SHA256 digest of the original value using the supplied secret key. The
same original value and key always produce the same masked value. Empty values
remain empty.
}

